  "raw_text": "228\n\nSugar siknis\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \ndiabetes\n \n/ diabetes\n\nSuk sirpi\n \n(a/t:\n \nSuki sirpi\n,\n \nSuk\n)\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nstork\n \n/ cigüeña\n\nSuk tara\n \n(a/t:\n \nSuki tara\n,\n \nSuk\n)\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \ncrane (bird)\n \n/ grulla (ave)\n\nSukia\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nwitch, fortune-teller, witch-doctor, sorcerer, medicine man\n \n/ bruja, adivina, brujo, hechicero, curandero\n\n(Construct:\n \nSukika\n)\n\nSukia lâka\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nspiritism, sorcery, witchcraft, magic\n \n/ espiritismo, brujería, magia\n\nSukling\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \ntoad\n \n/\n \nsapo\n\nSukutbaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto scoop, to dig, to undermine, to pinch, to touch with the finger\n \n/ sacar, cavar, socavar, pellizcar, tocar\ncon el dedo\n \nCheck to see how commonly used\n\nSukwaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto rot, to decay, to ripen, to fatten, to develop a sore or infection\n \n/ pudrirse, descomponerse, madurar,\nengordar, desarrollar una llaga o infección\n\nSukwan\n \n(v\n-\n3p\n-\npast/pasado, adj)\n \n–\n \nripened, rot, ripe, rotten\n \n/ madura, pudre, maduro/madura, podrido/podrida\n\nSukwanka\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nsore, ulcer, wound\n \n/ dolor, úlcera, herida\n\n(Ex/Ej(\ndb-Aiseya 53:5\n):\n \nwitin ai wîna sukwanka nani ba mita yawan nani wan rakan\n \n–\n \nbecause of his (body’s) wounds, we\n\nhealed\n \n/ debido a sus heridas (del cuerpo), sanamos)\n\nSul\n \n(\ndb,mwb,sgd,lfb,fy,km\n;\n \nSol\n-\nbh,lv,sp,sn\n) (n/s)\n \n–\n \nsoul\n \n/ alma\n\n(Construct:\n \nSulki, Solki\n;\n \nSulkam, Solkam\n;\n \nSulka, Solka\n)\n\n(Ex/Ej(\ndb\n-\nAiseya 53:11\n):\n \nAi\n \nsulka sari\n \n–\n \nsadness of his soul\n \n/ tristeza de su alma\n)\n\nSolka pruaikas\n \n–\n \nimmortal soul\n \n/ alma inmortal\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nsp\n-\n14\n):\n \nMan Baibil ba aisi kaiks ta wina tnata kat, bara aima kumira sin “solka ba pruaikas” bila ba sakma apia.\n \n–\n \nIf\n\nyou read the\n \nBible from the beginning to the end, you will not one time find the words “immortal soul”.\n \n/ Si lees la Biblia\n\ndesde el principio hasta el final, no encontrarás las palabras \"alma inmortal\".\n)\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nsp\n-\n14\n):\n \nBaibil ba marikisa solka ba pruaikas apia sa\n \n–\n \nThe Bible shows that the soul is not immortal\n \n/ La Biblia\n\nmuestra que el alma no es inmortal\n)\n\nSula\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \ndeer\n \n/ ciervo\n\nSuldiar\n \n(\ndb,my,lfb\n;\n \nSuldawa\n-\nbw,dba,lrw,bh,bm,lv,sn,dict,dictu\n;\n \nSuldawa\n,\nSuldiar\n-\nkm\n;\n \nSoldawa\n,\nSoldia\n,\nSoldiar\n,\nSuldia\n,\n\nSuldiar\n,\nSuldaho\n-\ndict\n-\nalt,dictu\n-\nalt\n;\n \nSoldiar\n,\nSuldiar\n,\nSuldahu\n-\ndbta\n-\nHeb\n;\n \nWardia\n-\ndbta\n-\nGrk\n)\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nsoldier\n \n/ soldado\n\n(Construct:\n \nSuldiarka\n-my,lfb\n;\n \nSuldawika\n-bm,lv,sn\n)\n\nSuliar\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nworkman, soldier, laborer\n, employee\n \n/ trabajador, soldado\n, empleado\n\nGabamint suliarka\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \ngovernment employee\n \n/ empl\neado del gobierno\n\nSul\np\na\n \n(\na/t\n:\n \nSulfa\n)\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nsulfur\n \n/ azufre\n\nSumi\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \njar, pitcher, clay\n \npot\n, iron pot\n \n/ jarra, olla de barro, olla de hierro\n\n(\nEx/Ej\n(\nmwb\n-\n02/19\n):\n \nJob sumi kriwan\n \npîska kum ni ai\n \ntaya\n \nba kurbi kan\n \n–\n \nJob was scratching himself from a broken piece of a jar\n \n/\n\nJob se rascaba\n \ncon\n \nun trozo roto de un frasco\n)\n\nSlaubla sumika\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nclay jar\n \n/ jarra de arcilla\n\nSumi papaskra\n \n(n\n-\nagent/s\n-\nagente)\n \n–\n \npotter\n \n/ alfarero\n\n(\nEx/Ej\n(\nfy116\n):\n \nSumi Papaskra Tara Jehova\n \n–\n \nGreat Potter Jehovah\n \n/ Gran Alfarero Jehová\n)\n\nSumura\n \n(\ndict,dictu\n-\nalt\n;\n \nSumruru\n-\ndictu\n;\n \nSumura\n-\ndict\n-\nalt, dictu\n-\nalt\n;\n \nSumruro\n-\ndict\n-\nalt\n;\n \nSumrura\n-\ndictu\n-\nalt\n;\n \nSumuru\n-\ndictu\n-\n\nalt\n;\n \nSumur\n-\ntc\n)\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nhat, helmet\n \n/ sombrero, casco\n\n(Construct(\ndict,db\n):\n \nSumurki\n;\n \nSumurkam\n;\n \nSumurka\n)\n\n(Note/Nota: Most commonly used:\n \nSumura, Sumur\n \n/ Más comúnmente utilizado:\n \nSumura, Sumur\n)\n\nSunaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto raise up, to save up, to raise, to ascend, to mount, to put up\n \n/ elevar, ahorrar, ascender, montar, soportar\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nfy18\n):\n \nbank kum ra lalah suni briaia\n \n–\n \nto save up money in a bank\n \n/ ahorrar dinero en un banco)\n\nKaina sunaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto help, to look after, to care for\n \n/ ayudar, cuidar\n\n(Ex/Ej(\ndb-Jirimaya 1:8\n):\n \nkainam sunaia\n \n–\n \nto care for you\n \n/ cuidarte)\n\nPura sunaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto pray, to raise above, to put above\n \n/ orar, rezar, elevar por encima, poner por encima\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nhf30\n):\n \nYawan wan pura sunisa taim Gȃd wal aisisa, ban sakuna witin ra sin yawan walaia sa.\n \n–\n \nWhen we pray, we\nspeak with God, but we must listen to Him also.\n \n/ Cuando oramos, hablamos con Dios, pero también debemos\nescucharlo)\n\nPura sasunra\n \n(n-agent/s-agente)\n \n–\n \nperson who prays\n \n/ persona que ore\n\nPura suni makabaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto ask in prayer\n \n/ pedir en oración\n\nPura suni makabi kaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto be asking in prayer\n \n/ estar pidiendo en oración\n\nPura sunra\n \n(n\n-\nconcept form / s\n-\nforma concepto)\n \n–\n \nprayer\n \n/ oración",
